# Delivery standards

Any implementation work in this repo must follow `.cursor/skills/delivery-standards/SKILL.md` (also `.claude/skills/delivery-standards/SKILL.md`).

## Required on every code change

1. **TDD-first** — failing test(s) before implementation for `src/main/`, `src/preload/`, IPC, and other testable logic.
2. **Verify before done** — all must pass; do not report completion otherwise:
   - `npm run lint:fix` then `npm run format`
   - `npm run lint`
   - `npm run format:check`
   - `npm test`
   - `npm run type-check`
   - `npm run deadcode`
   - `npm run test:diff-coverage`
   - `npm run fireguard` (when unit tests added/changed — grade must not be F)
   - `npm run build` (when renderer/build output is affected)
   - `npm run electron-build` (when main/preload changed)
3. **Board traceability** — create a ticket in `/board/backlog/` or update the related epic/ticket before or as you start. If the user named a ticket id, use `complete-ticket` skill.
4. **Red-team review** — run `.cursor/skills/red-team-review/SKILL.md` before marking work done or merge-ready (see `.cursor/rules/red-team-review.mdc`).

## Also required

- Read `README.md` and `ARCHITECTURE.md` for architecture boundaries.
- Check off acceptance criteria only after verification; move tickets to `done/` when complete.
- Do not commit unless the user explicitly asks.

## Exceptions

- Read-only answers with no code changes: no ticket or test gate required.
